/Subject (Climate hazard\054 polluted air\054 water stress\054 hunger and weak institutions strike the same people at the same time\054 and no single response reaches them all\056 This report sets out the H Heuristics Framework for Polycrisis Resilience\054 a development\055oriented strategy that reduces vulnerability before a crisis\054 strengthens adaptation during it\054 and plans for conditions that persist or cannot be prevented\056 The framework is presented as developed by Hunter Hughes\054 Founder of H Heuristics\056 It is structured as one objective \050reducing human and systemic vulnerability\051\054 two complementary tracks \050proactive transformation and adaptive capacity\051\054 a third dimension of reactive resilience\054 and six application pillars\072 sustainable convergence\054 diffusion of innovations\054 targeted risk reduction\054 human development and vulnerability reduction\054 resilient infrastructure and institutions\054 and long\055term adaptation and survivability\056)
/Title (The H Heuristics Framework for Polycrisis Resilience\072 Formal Framework and Application for the 21st Century)
/Trapped null
